<!-- HERO -->
<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">KV Cache</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">LLM Inference</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Can I Buy Your KV Cache?</h1>
  <p class="lead">Right now, millions of AI agents are reading the same documents — and each one recomputes them from scratch, re-running prefill, the most expensive step a large model takes, over identical text. This paper makes an almost offensively simple proposal: compute the KV cache <em>once</em>, let a publisher host it, and let every other agent <em>buy</em> the right to load it and skip prefill. It's token-exact, and on Qwen3-4B it's 9–50× cheaper than prefilling.</p>
